# Always Report a Terminal GitHub Status

Any play that posts a `pending` status via `demo.lightwell.report_status` must
guarantee a terminal `success`/`failure` status gets posted too, even when a
step fails with an unhandled task error (not just an expected/graceful
failure condition). Otherwise the GitHub commit/PR check hangs on `pending`
forever.

Wrap the risky steps (build, deploy, health check, rollback, etc.) in a
`block`/`rescue`/`always`:

- `rescue` catches hard task failures and records a failure fact (e.g.
  `health_check_passed: false`, plus a short `*_failure_reason` for the
  status description). Don't put secrets or raw error text in the reason --
  it's posted to a public GitHub status.
- `always` (or a step immediately after the block) posts the final status
  and re-raises/fails so the AAP job itself is also marked failed, not just
  the GitHub check.

## Example

```yaml
- name: Deploy, verify, and roll back the application
  block:
    - name: Deploy the application
      ansible.builtin.include_role:
        name: demo.lightwell.deploy_app
    - name: Run the post-deploy health check
      ansible.builtin.include_role:
        name: demo.lightwell.health_check
  rescue:
    - name: Record that deployment failed unexpectedly
      ansible.builtin.set_fact:
        health_check_passed: false
        deploy_failure_reason: "failed unexpectedly -- see AAP job output for details"
  always:
    - name: Report the final GitHub status check result
      vars:
        github_status_state: "{{ 'success' if health_check_passed else 'failure' }}"
        github_status_description: "{{ deploy_failure_reason | default('...') }}"
      ansible.builtin.include_role:
        name: demo.lightwell.report_status
```

When referencing facts inside the `always`/status-description Jinja
expression that are normally set earlier in the `block` (e.g.
`initial_health_check_passed`), guard them with `| default(...)` since
`rescue` may trigger before they're ever assigned.
